---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const lastUpdated = 'August 17, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Delete Your Voxivium Account — Voxivium"
  description="How to request deletion of your Voxivium account and data, what gets deleted, what is kept, and for how long."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Delete Your Account', path: '/legal/delete-account' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Delete your Voxivium account</h1>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class="lead">
          This page explains how to request deletion of your <strong>Voxivium</strong> account and
          the data associated with it. Voxivium is published by <strong>Voxivium, PBC</strong>, a
          Delaware Public Benefit Corporation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="prose">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="callout">
          <h2 id="steps">How to request account deletion</h2>
          <p>You can delete your account yourself, from inside the app, at any time.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open the <strong>Voxivium</strong> app and sign in.</li>
            <li>Tap your <strong>profile icon</strong> in the top bar to open the account menu.</li>
            <li>
              Scroll to the <strong>Danger zone</strong> section and tap
              <strong>"Delete my account."</strong>
            </li>
            <li>
              Read the confirmation steps. They explain what deletion does and offer alternatives
              such as leaving your account dormant. You can stop at any point.
            </li>
            <li>
              On the final screen, tap <strong>"Delete my account"</strong> to confirm. Your account
              is deleted immediately and you are signed out on that device.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <h3>If you can't sign in</h3>
        <p>
          If you have lost access to your account and cannot complete the steps above, email <a
            href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
          > from the address associated with your account and ask us to delete it. We will verify that
          you control the account before acting on the request, and we complete verified requests within
          30 days.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what-is-deleted">What is deleted</h2>
        <p>
          Deletion happens in two stages: an immediate stage when you confirm, and a permanent
          purge 30 days later.
        </p>

        <h3>Immediately, when you confirm</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Your identity record is anonymized.</strong> Your name, residential address,
            date of birth, phone number, and email address are erased from your account record and
            replaced with non-identifying placeholders. Your sign-in credential link is removed, so
            the account can no longer be accessed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your civic input stops counting.</strong> Your belief stances, importance
            ratings, and stances on legislation, executive orders, and court rulings are removed
            from all district and national aggregates. Any unsaved draft beliefs are deleted
            outright.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your account is marked deleted</strong> and can no longer be signed in to.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Permanently, 30 days after you confirm</h3>
        <p>
          A scheduled job removes the remaining records from our production systems. This includes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your account record and your voter record.</li>
          <li>
            Your profile data: first and last name, residential address, date of birth, political
            party affiliation, gender, and race or ethnicity if you chose to provide it.
          </li>
          <li>Your identity verification result and your voter registration verification result.</li>
          <li>Your assigned voter districts and voter registration history.</li>
          <li>
            All of your civic input: belief stances, importance ratings, poll responses, and stances
            on legislation, executive orders, and court rulings.
          </li>
          <li>Your cached report card and any account role or account-issue records.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The 30-day window exists so that a deletion made by mistake, or by someone who gained
          access to your device, can be reversed by contacting <a
            href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
          >. After 30 days, deletion cannot be undone.
        </p>

        <h3>Backups</h3>
        <p>
          Deleted data is purged from encrypted backups within <strong>90 days</strong> of the
          deletion request. Backups are not used to restore deleted accounts.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what-is-kept">What is kept, and for how long</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>A record that a deletion occurred.</strong> We keep a security audit entry
            noting that an account deletion happened, along with the time, the originating IP
            address, and a pseudonymous identifier. It does not contain your name, address, or
            email. We keep it to protect accounts against unauthorized deletion.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Aggregated, anonymized statistics.</strong> Statistics previously derived from
            civic input and disclosed to customers are not individually identifiable and are not
            recalled from those customers. Your future contribution to those statistics stops
            immediately on deletion.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Records we are legally required to keep.</strong> We may retain limited
            information, such as transaction and billing records, for as long as tax, accounting, or
            fraud-prevention law requires.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Marketing email signups.</strong> If you joined our email list through
            voxivium.com, that is a separate record from your app account. To remove it, use the
            unsubscribe link in any message or email <a href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com"
              >privacy@voxivium.com</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Voxivium does not collect or store your government-issued identity documents at any point,
          so there are none to delete. Identity verification is performed by a third-party provider;
          we retain only the result.
        </p>

        <h2 id="deleting-some-data">Deleting some data without deleting your account</h2>
        <p>
          You do not have to delete your account to remove or change individual data. From inside
          the app you can edit or clear the profile fields you provided, and you can change or
          remove your stance on any belief, bill, executive order, or court ruling at any time. A
          removed stance stops counting toward district and national aggregates.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some data cannot be removed while your account remains open, because the service depends
          on it: your email address, your identity verification result, and your voter registration
          status and districts are required to keep an account eligible. To remove those, delete the
          account.
        </p>
        <p>
          For any deletion request that the app does not cover, email <a
            href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
          >. We honor verified requests within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2 id="subscriptions">Subscriptions</h2>
        <p>
          Deleting your account does <strong>not</strong> cancel a paid subscription. Subscriptions
          are billed by the store or processor you purchased through, and must be canceled there:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Play:</strong> Play Store → profile icon → Payments &amp; subscriptions →
            Subscriptions → Voxivium → Cancel subscription.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Apple App Store:</strong> Settings → your name → Subscriptions → Voxivium →
            Cancel Subscription.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>PayPal:</strong> Settings → Payments → Manage automatic payments → Voxivium →
            Cancel.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>Cancel the subscription before deleting your account, so billing stops.</p>

        <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
        <div class="contact">
          Voxivium, PBC<br />
          Privacy: <a href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a><br />
          Support: <a href="mailto:support@voxivium.com">support@voxivium.com</a><br />
          Full policy: <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 10vh, 6rem) 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .meta {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text4);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .lead {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .prose {
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.625rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--color-brand-text2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .prose ul,
  .prose ol {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .prose li::marker {
    color: var(--color-brand-text4);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .prose a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--color-brand-text1);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* The deletion steps are what Google's reviewer and a departing user both
     come here for. Give them a bordered block at the top of the page rather
     than letting them read as one section among many. */
  .callout {
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el2);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .callout h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .callout ol {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .contact {
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-brand-el1);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
